  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Endless relay – catch the team ahead",
  "description": "Four cones make a box of about 10 × 10 metres. Split the players into two to four teams, each standing at its own corner. The first in each team skates with the puck one lap around the box, outside the cones, and hands over to the next in the team with a high five. Then they go to the back.\n\nThe relay goes on until someone catches the skater from another team, or for a set number of laps. Short, intense bursts with rest in between – good for keeping the tempo up for longer. Leave the pucks out if you only want to work on skating. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Full speed the whole lap – you rest in the line."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the puck close in the turns around the cones."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Next in line: be ready with your stick on the ice."
    }
  ],
